summary:
  The capture shell goes from its free-space check straight to the stream and
  never looks for the stop mark first.

history:
  A stop read the pid file once. While the shell was still at its mkdir or df
  there was no pid, nothing was signalled, and the shell went on to record.
  Measured 2026-11-10 with the real command and df held back: no pid file at
  Stop, the stream asked for afterwards, 159819 bytes written, rc=0. A stop
  now leaves a mark, and the shell reads it before it asks for the stream.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
                  + "if off; then cln; echo __REC_OFF__; exit 0; fi; "

replace:
                  + "if false; then cln; echo __REC_OFF__; exit 0; fi; "

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_the_capture_reads_the_mark_before_the_stream_and_after_the_pid
  and tests/test_recording_stop_race.py::test_a_stop_during_the_preparation_records_nothing.
  Line-neutral.
